# The CodeTracer Embed SDK the Client SDK is built and checked against.
#
# WHAT THIS PIN IS
# ----------------
# `CODETRACER_REF` names the exact `metacraft-labs/codetracer` commit whose
# `src/frontend/viewmodel/` tree IS the Embed SDK for this repository. It is
# ONE place, read by `.github/workflows/ci.yml` for both of its jobs, and it is
# what `$CODETRACER_SRC` points at for every cross-repo check here:
# `ci/test/embed-handoff-test.sh`, `ci/test/viewmodel-seam-test.sh`,
# `ci/test/client-sdk-boundary.sh --require-embed` and the CHAIN_TOKENS
# cross-check inside `ci/test/client-sdk-boundary-test.sh`. One value, so the
# version the handoff compiles against, the version the seam suite runs
# against, and the version the boundary guard scans can never be three
# different things.
#
# WHY A COMMIT AND NOT A BRANCH NAME
# ----------------------------------
# `CODETRACER_BRANCH` below records which branch the commit is on — `dev`, the
# Embed SDK's mainline, where the facade (`codetracer_embed.nim`), its
# `DebuggerSession` and `TraceSource` landed as `b2fc33c9` and everything since
# has followed. But CI checks out the COMMIT, not the branch, because a branch
# name is not a fact about bytes: a push to `codetracer` `dev` would silently
# change what this repository's green build was green against, and the build
# would not even know it had moved. A green build here has to be able to name
# the bytes it was green against, and this line is that name. `CODETRACER_BRANCH`
# is documentation and a starting point for the next bump; nothing reads it.
#
# HOW TO MOVE IT
# --------------
# Moving the pin forward is a deliberate edit of this one line, and the four
# things it must survive are, in the order of what they cost to run:
#
#   ci/test/client-sdk-boundary.sh --require-embed   (that Embed SDK still
#                                                     carries no chain concept)
#   ci/test/client-sdk-boundary-test.sh              (the two repositories still
#                                                     agree on CHAIN_TOKENS)
#   ci/test/embed-handoff-test.sh --require          (the handoff still compiles
#                                                     against that Embed SDK)
#   just viewmodel-seam                              (the degraded-state wire
#                                                     spellings have not drifted)
#
# All four need `CODETRACER_SRC` on a checkout of the commit below — validate
# against the PIN, not against whatever a sibling `../codetracer` happens to be
# sitting on. Nothing else in this repository needs to change.
# MOVED for hydration (2026-08-29). The previous value,
# `86719698e0ea49af7e985cfa6a043001dfdede5a`, does NOT contain
# `src/frontend/viewmodel/backend/worker_backend.nim`: `WorkerBackendService`
# landed later, in `476d2d36e57a49663faa0385e2f9363c8e89fb99` ("feat(sdk):
# WorkerBackendService — DAP over postMessage to the WASM replay worker"), of
# which 86719698 is an ancestor. `client/hydrate/` compiles against that
# adapter, so a pin below it cannot build the hydration bundle at all —
# `client/hydrate/build.sh` checks for the file by name and says so, rather
# than letting Nim report a missing internal module.
#
# The value below is `origin/dev`'s tip at the time of the move. It also
# carries the engine-side fixes hydration depends on and the
# `backend/dap_dialect.md` that documents the remaining gaps.
#
# MOVED for the event-log decode (2026-09-17). `client/hydrate/live_navigation`
# carried a PRIVATE copy of the `ct/updated-events` decode, written when the
# SDK had none: at 8d1c84a8 the store's only event-log entry point was
# `applyMarkerRowsResponse`, which writes `markerRows`, a signal
# `projectEventLog` does not read. `af70456c9` makes `ReplayDataStore` the one
# conversion point — `eventLogRowFromJson` / `eventLogRowsFromJson` name the
# bare array THIS event carries as one of the three envelopes they read, and
# `EventLogVM.eventRows` is now an alias of `store.eventLog.rows` rather than a
# second signal. `live_navigation` calls that decoder; it does not exist at the
# previous pin, so the module does not compile below this one (measured:
# "undeclared identifier: 'eventLogRowsFromJson'").
#
# The four gates this line must survive were run against the value below, on a
# `../codetracer` checkout of exactly that commit, and all four passed:
#
#   ci/test/client-sdk-boundary.sh --require-embed   10 checks, 0 failing
#   ci/test/client-sdk-boundary-test.sh              44 cases, 44 passed
#   ci/test/embed-handoff-test.sh --require          11 tests, all OK
#   just viewmodel-seam                              18 tests, all OK
#
# and so did `just debug-panes`, which is what actually exercises the decode,
# and `client/hydrate/build.sh --require` with all three sources at their pins.
#
# THE FOUR GATES ABOVE ARE NOT THE WHOLE LIST, and this move is the evidence.
# Two vendor checks also track this value and neither is named in it:
#
#   ci/test/flow-layout-vendor.sh    Part A asserts the vendor manifest's
#                                    commit EQUALS this line. Moving the pin
#                                    without re-vendoring fails it by
#                                    construction. Re-vendored in this change:
#                                    upstream's `flow_layout.nim` moved
#                                    b089e9a6 -> db6d4d40, a doc comment only
#                                    (0 non-comment lines changed), and part B
#                                    re-confirmed every observable agrees.
#
#   ci/test/layout-model-vendor.sh   FIXED ON 2026-09-17, in the change that
#                                    also re-vendored the layout model. Read
#                                    this because it is the WORKED EXAMPLE of
#                                    how a vendor pin goes wrong.
#
#                                    It had been a BLOCKING step of the
#                                    `viewmodels` job and RED BY CONSTRUCTION.
#                                    The cause was a category error, not a
#                                    defect upstream: part A pinned the copy to
#                                    the MODULE's own mainline (`eb1776ea`)
#                                    while part B compared it against whatever
#                                    `$CODETRACER_SRC` is — i.e. THIS pin. Two
#                                    different commits by design, so the gate
#                                    asked a question with no passable answer
#                                    and reddened on every SDK bump whether or
#                                    not that module had moved.
#
#                                    The visible symptom was a compile error,
#                                    and it MASKED the answer. Part B copied
#                                    each side into a flat directory, which
#                                    broke `layout_model.nim`'s relative import
#                                    of `../../common/contributed_pane_id`, so
#                                    the probe said "the conformance probe
#                                    failed" — a sentence about a broken script
#                                    — for what was really a moved schema.
#                                    Mounted at its own depth the probe reports
#                                    four genuine divergences at this pin:
#
#                                      LayoutSchemaVersion   vendored 1, up 3
#                                      defaultReplayLayout   upstream adds
#                                                            `"docked":[]`
#                                      PaneKind              upstream adds
#                                                            `fileTree`,
#                                                            `buildOutput`
#                                      validate()            upstream's result
#                                                            gains `contributed`
#
#                                    WHAT THAT COST THE SITE: nothing, and that
#                                    was MEASURED rather than argued. The debug
#                                    route walks `blockTracerReplayLayout()`,
#                                    not `defaultReplayLayout()`; shipping code
#                                    calls neither `saveLayout` nor `validate`
#                                    nor reads `LayoutSchemaVersion`; and the
#                                    eleven existing `PaneKind` spellings kept
#                                    their order, so every `pane-*` element id
#                                    a deep link or the capture harness
#                                    addresses is unchanged. Exporting before
#                                    and after the re-vendor produced 931
#                                    byte-identical files. The one real change
#                                    was the two new enum members, which
#                                    `components/debugger.paneBody` is
#                                    deliberately total over — it broke the
#                                    build, which is that `case`'s stated job,
#                                    and both are now named as panes this site
#                                    does not place.
#
#                                    THE PIN IS NOW THE FIX. The manifest names
#                                    THIS commit, exactly as the flow manifest
#                                    does, and part A asserts the equality. So
#                                    a red part B from here on means upstream
#                                    really changed the module, with a diff to
#                                    read — and moving this line without
#                                    re-vendoring fails part A by name rather
#                                    than failing part B for a reason that is
#                                    not about the module at all.
CODETRACER_REPO=metacraft-labs/codetracer
CODETRACER_REF=af70456c981ea8e3c8de2534cdee16eca5550efd
CODETRACER_BRANCH=dev

# The IsoNim / nim-everywhere sources the Embed SDK's own graph needs
# (`isonim/core/signals`, `isonim/viewmodel`, `isonim/testing/test_utils`).
# Kept in lock-step with flake.nix's pinned inputs.
ISONIM_REPO=metacraft-labs/isonim
ISONIM_REF=03f8349784b2642ba5b49101f1a04b454b3476f3
NIM_EVERYWHERE_REPO=metacraft-labs/nim-everywhere
NIM_EVERYWHERE_REF=b2ce1c6b31743c4351aff4ad835f385f79b70edd
